{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/pulls/927","id":4200012640,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSbOoU876Vxtg","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/927","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/927.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/927.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/927","number":927,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Require tool-result evidence before general-change completion","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n- preserve explicit tool failure metadata across OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic, and Responses inputs\n- separate observed attempts from successful planner steps, recover one rejected write with read + bounded retry, preserve the primary write when an auxiliary plan write fails, and stop honestly on repeated or verification failures\n- require successful verification output to match the requested bytes before reporting completion\n- seed mismatch/unverified responses in all five supported languages and refresh generated closure/self-AST evidence\n\nCloses #905.\n\n## Reproduction and root cause\n\nThe reported prompt, `Create a file hello.txt containing exactly: Hello World`, reproduced three defects: the shorter equal-start marker left `exactly:` in the payload; provider error metadata was discarded while every tool result counted as completed; and the general planner emitted success based on call counts without checking result status or output.\n\nThe pre-fix focused suite retained in `docs/case-studies/issue-905/test-evidence/regression-red.log` fails 6 of 7 assertions. Both original Agent CLI provider traces and authenticated issue/PR snapshots are retained in the case study. This is a protocol/state bug, so no visual screenshot applies.\n\n## Relationship to `main`\n\nWhile this branch was open, `main` landed its own fixes for the three defects named in the original issue text: `strip_clause_lead` in `src/agentic_coding/general_planner.rs` (control-phrase parsing) and `ShellEnvelope`/`failed_verification` in `src/agentic_coding/tool_result.rs` (exit-code-aware failure reporting). Those implementations are kept as-is by this merge; the branch's earlier, narrower versions were dropped.\n\nWhat remains unique to this pull request is the requirement added by the qwen trace in the issue comment — `is_error: true` tool results were being discarded entirely, so the plan advanced over a step that never ran:\n\n- `ChatMessage::is_error` on the shared protocol type, populated from Anthropic `tool_result.is_error`, Responses `is_error`/`isError`/failed `status`, and the OpenAI-compatible `is_error`/`isError` fields\n- `Progress` recording observed attempts separately from satisfied steps, so a rejected call cannot count as progress\n- the two-turn `read_file` → `write_file` recovery the issue comment asked for, bounded per target path\n- content-match verification: literal completion compares transport-normalized command output against the request-derived payload\n- `general_execution.rs`, the plan's execution state machine, split out of the planner\n\n## Verification\n\nLatest run, on the merge commit that brings `origin/main` (`15ecff15`, v0.329.1) into the branch:\n\n- `cargo test --test unit` — 2552 passed, 0 failed, 3 ignored\n- `cargo test --test unit issue_905` — 15 passed\n- `cargo test --test integration -- --test-threads=1` — 306 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored (serialized to respect the local runner's socket limit)\n- `cargo test --tests --examples` — passed\n- `cargo fmt --check`; `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`\n- `scripts/audit-total-closure.py` — `UNRESOLVED distinct: 0  occurrences: 0`\n- `check-file-size`, `check-associative-terminology`, `check-hardcoded-language`, `check-disk-usage-policy`, `check-worker-line-budget`, `check-changelog-fragment` — all passed\n- write-effect ladder against a locally built release server — 9/9 rungs, `baseline 9/9 -> now 9/9`; judge unit tests — 20 passed\n\nGenerated artifacts (self-AST census, planner fixtures, total-closure shards) were regenerated from the merged sources, so they remain pure functions of `src/**` and `data/seed/**`.\n\nRegression coverage includes the exact prompt, 20 parsing variants, Qwen-style explicit errors, Codex-style nonzero exits, bounded write recovery, wrong/matching verification evidence, requested failure vocabulary, and Anthropic/Responses parity. Acceptance traceability is in `docs/case-studies/issue-905/requirements.md`.\n\n## Same-task self-application\n\nFormal AI served the `formal-ai` model to the external Agent CLI in session `ses_034e9dafeffe7nxeTkFhmHLmZN`, which authored and read back the canonical tool-result evidence invariant. That is 1 of 5 reviewed smallest leaves (20%). Session `ses_03474fd81ffeMofsJrUWdYDEEd` refreshed the planner-derived self-healing fixture through the same real client/server path. Replay harnesses and byte-identical artifacts are retained under `experiments/issue_905_*` and `docs/case-studies/issue-905/`.\n\nAn earlier whole-issue attempt selected an unsupported hosted fallback and received HTTP 401 before Formal AI executed. It is retained as failed infrastructure evidence and is not counted as authorship; echoed authorization headers are redacted.\n\n\n## Write-effect ladder regression (fixed)\n\nThe issue #916 write-effect ladder, which `main` added while this branch was open, failed rung R916-01 on the first push of the merged branch: `dishonest report=['reported failure although every declared effect landed']`, baseline 9/9 → 8/9.\n\nRoot cause: R916-01 replays the exact issue #905 transport fault (`write_stdin failed: Unknown process id 0`, bytes never land). This branch's recovery path exhausted its bounded per-path retries and then reported the transport message directly, without ever running the check the plan itself had named — so the run ended in a failure report that no observed exit code backed.\n\nFix: once write recovery is exhausted, run the named verification once; its exit status is what the report carries. Locally the ladder is back to 9/9 (`baseline 9/9 -> now 9/9`), and `an_unrecoverable_write_still_asks_the_workspace_before_reporting` pins the behavior in the unit suite.\n","created_at":"2026-08-04T03:59:39Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T06:29:47Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"a551b981c395be5be4be6d30b5e3fdf0baab762f","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.g